  "hop_decay_finding": {
    "result": "bit-identical metrics at 0.35/0.45/0.55/0.65/0.75",
    "reason": "combine() applies base * hop_decay**hop; at depth=1 every hop-1 node receives the same multiplier, so the relative order within the hop-1 set cannot change. hop_decay can only matter at depth>=2, which Step 10 showed contributes nothing under max_nodes=100.",
    "joint_experiment": "degenerate at depth 1 \u2014 any top_k x hop_decay grid collapses onto the top_k curve, so no grid was run (spec \u00a710/\u00a711)"
  },
